jules: Quick note—hit a few `Unexpected end of JSON input` errors in the node SDK when streaming with SSE. Repro in onboarding sample-app (node 18 + @redwood/sdk-js v0.6.x). Seems to spike when users close the tab or when auth rotates mid-stream. Anyone else?

sam: yes. Node's current handler assumes each SSE `data:` event is delivered atomically in a single 'data' callback. That's not safe; proxies/TCP can split events.

vikas: can you paste a minimal repro and the raw bytes? I'll add a unit test. /cc @tori for runtime rotate behavior.

jules: minimal repro: ```js
// naive parse that breaks on split chunks
res.on('data', chunk => {
  const s = chunk.toString();
  const events = s.split('\n\n');
  events.forEach(e => {
    if (e.startsWith('data: ')) {
      const payload = JSON.parse(e.slice(6)); // throws when split mid-json
      onEvent(payload);
    }
  });
});
```
error: `SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input`

tori: runtime note: when we rotate auth we may close the socket and open a fresh one. We currently don't emit any resume metadata. That means partial bytes in-flight are lost unless the client persists trailing bytes across reconnect.

sam: two approaches: 1) server adds sequence/resume control events so clients can detect gaps, or 2) SDK preserves a trailing buffer across reconnects and only JSON.parse when full `

` delimiter seen. Both are useful.

vikas: SDK parity item: node sdk doesn't persist the trailing tail across reconnects. Plan: add a tiny persistent tail buffer that is kept between reconnect attempts, split on full `\n\n`, and only JSON.parse complete events. Also add unit/integration tests that simulate: mid-event client close, forced auth rotate, and proxy chunking. Will also add a telemetry counter `sse_parse_error`.

jules: for onboarding docs I'll add a recommended snippet showing a persistent buffer and safe parse with try/catch. Also mention bumping token TTL as a short-term mitigation for long-lived streams.

tori: runtime action: we'll try to emit an optional pre-rotate control event for planned rotates: `event: control
data: {"type":"pre_rotate","last_seq": 1024}

` and on new stream emit a resume echo. For forced 401s we'll attempt to include resume metadata on the new stream. I'll open a PR with shape suggestions.

vikas: follow-ups: 1) implement tail buffer + tests in node SDK, 2) add optional strict-seq mode if server provides `seq` in payloads (SDK will detect gaps and emit `sse_resume_gap` telemetry), 3) update sample-app and quickstart docs with robust parse snippet. ETA: patch + tests tomorrow.

ci-bot: Created issue #4501: "sdk-js(node): SSE partial-chunk parse error - tail buffer + seq handling" assigned to vikas.

jules: thanks—assigning follow-ups: vikas (sdk patch/tests/telemetry), tori (runtime pre-rotate PR), me (docs/sample-app). Will smoke test once PRs land. :thumbsup:
